To print all unique rows of a given matrix, we can use a set to keep track of unique rows encountered while iterating through the matrix. As we iterate through each row, we convert it into a string representation and add it to the set. If the row is already present in the set, it means it's a duplicate and can be skipped. Otherwise, it's a unique row that we print.
