**A3**
You can achieve this using Spring AOP by defining an aspect that intercepts method calls and logs the execution time.
**For example**
The LoggingAspect will intercept all methods in the MyService class and log their execution time.

```java
@Aspect
@Component
public class LoggingAspect {

    @Around("execution(* com.example.service.*.*(..))")
    public Object logExecutionTime(ProceedingJoinPoint joinPoint) throws Throwable {
        long start = System.currentTimeMillis();

        Object proceed = joinPoint.proceed();

        long executionTime = System.currentTimeMillis() - start;
        System.out.println(joinPoint.getSignature() + " executed in " + executionTime + "ms");
        return proceed;
    }
}

@Service
public class MyService {

    public void someMethod() {
        // Method logic
    }

    public void anotherMethod() {
        // Method logic
    }
}
