Versioning in a Spring Boot application, especially for REST APIs, is essential to ensure backward compatibility and allow clients to smoothly transition between different versions of your API. There are several ways to implement versioning in a Spring Boot application:
- URI Versioning
- Request Parameter Versioning
- Header Versioning
- Content Negotiation Versioning
