Question: Create an event emitter that can subscribe and unsubscribe to any event,…
Question: Create an event emitter that can subscribe and unsubscribe to any event, synchronously and asynchronously.
**EventEmitter Implementation**
**Synchronous example**
**Asynchronous Example**
- Subscribe to Events: Add multiple listeners for an event.
- Unsubscribe from Events: Remove a specific listener for an event.
- Synchronous Emission: Call listeners synchronously.
- Asynchronous Emission: Call listeners asynchronously using Promise.

```javascript
class EventEmitter {
  constructor() {
    this.events = {}; // Store event listeners
  }

  /**
   * Subscribes a listener to a specific event.
   * @param {string} event - Name of the event
   * @param {function} listener - Callback function for the event
   */
  subscribe(event, listener) {
    if (!this.events[event]) {
      this.events[event] = [];
    }
    this.events[event].push(listener);
  }

  /**
   * Unsubscribes a listener from a specific event.
   * @param {string} event - Name of the event
   * @param {function} listener - Callback function to remove
   */
  unsubscribe(event, listener) {
    if (!this.events[event]) return;

    this.events[event] = this.events[event].filter((l) => l !== listener);

    // Clean up if no listeners remain
    if (this.events[event].length === 0) {
      delete this.events[event];
    }
  }

  /**
   * Emits an event synchronously, invoking all associated listeners.
   * @param {string} event - Name of the event
   * @param {...any} args - Arguments to pass to the listeners
   */
  emitSync(event, ...args) {
    if (!this.events[event]) return;

    this.events[event].forEach((listener) => {
      listener(...args);
    });
  }

  /**
   * Emits an event asynchronously, invoking all associated listeners.
   * @param {string} event - Name of the event
   * @param {...any} args - Arguments to pass to the listeners
   * @returns {Promise} - Resolves after all listeners have been invoked
   */
  async emitAsync(event, ...args) {
    if (!this.events[event]) return;

    const promises = this.events[event].map((listener) =>
      Promise.resolve().then(() => listener(...args))
    );
    await Promise.all(promises);
  }
}
```

```javascript
const emitter = new EventEmitter();

function syncListener(data) {
    console.log(`Sync Event Received: ${data}`);
}

// Subscribe to the event
emitter.subscribe('syncEvent', syncListener);

// Emit the event synchronously
emitter.emitSync('syncEvent', 'Hello, World!');

// Unsubscribe from the event
emitter.unsubscribe('syncEvent', syncListener);

// Emit again to verify it was unsubscribed
emitter.emitSync('syncEvent', 'This will not be logged.');
```

